  "summary": "The most striking pattern is that single‑planet systems have a higher mean orbital period (2641.63 days) and mass (3.33 M⊕) than multi‑planet systems (1191.73 days, 1.61 M⊕). Radial Velocity dominates detections (53.43 %) and shows a moderate multi‑system fraction (40.69 %). Transit detections, while fewer, have a very high missing‑mass rate (≈99 %). Correlations are weak and negative: number of planets is slightly inversely related to both orbital period (‑0.06) and mass (‑0.24). Missing mass is most common in single‑planet systems, especially for Transit and Imaging methods. All statistics exclude NULLs where appropriate and percentages are rounded to two decimals.",
